WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.260
"Do Alkaline Diets Help
Athletic Performance?"

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.980
Theoretically, bathing your muscles in
an alkaline environment should enable

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.180
faster acid removal from muscle
cells, delaying the muscle fatigue

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.520
that's due to the buildup
of lactic acid in the muscle.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.660
Given these buffering effects,
no wonder sodium bicarbonate —

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.600
in other words, baking soda —
has been found to have such

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.720
significant ergogenic
or performance-enhancing

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.880
effects on muscular endurance.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.660
The problem with loading with
baking soda is that it frequently

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.280
causes severe gastrointestinal
distress, and at standard doses

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.280
you could easily take in twice the
recommended upper daily limit

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:51.000
of sodium in just that one load.
Therefore, what about a low-acid diet,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.820
which focuses on high intakes
of fruits and vegetables?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.660
That may be an attractive
alternative to bicarbonate loading

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.360
for improving anaerobic
exercise performance,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.660
meaning short burst
activity like sprinting.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.440
Today's diets are acid-forming,
meaning higher in animal foods

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.300
with fewer vegetables and fruits,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.360
whereas in general, the alkaline-
promoting diet is centered around

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.860
whole plant foods, with few processed
foods and less meat, dairy and eggs,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.780
which are accepted as acid-forming
foods. Although alkalizing chemicals

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.160
such as sodium bicarbonate have
been shown to consistently improve

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.240
performance, alkalizing diets do
not demonstrate the same effect.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.820
A review of ten studies
that investigated

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.540
the effect of high versus low dietary
acid loads on athletic performance

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.500
did not find consistently improved
exercise performance

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.320
at maximal or submaximal
exercise intensities.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.488
However, maybe they just
didn't go alkaline enough?

00:01:48.488 --> 00:01:49.740
For example, in this study

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.540
they had people eat more
fruits and vegetables

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.580
and less meat, cheese,
cereals, and eggs,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.840
but saw no difference in any
performance-related parameters.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.060
But a sufficiently alkaline diet
is characterized by the production

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.800
of alkaline urine, a pH
of pee at least 7 or higher.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.200
And if you look at what
the participants achieved,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.180
most failed to meet
the benchmark,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.260
so their diet may just not have
been alkaline-forming enough.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.560
In this study showing enhanced
400-meter sprint performance,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.680
they were able to swap out
enough meat, eggs, cheese

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.860
and cereal products, and swap
in enough fruits and vegetables

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.800
that they were just barely
able to make 7,

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.160
and they did get a little performance
boost, suggesting that it's possible

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.360
to improve sprint performance by
consuming alkalizing natural foods

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.660
and beverages, without
the ingestion of baking soda.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.860
Thus, an alkalizing diet may be
an easy and natural way

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.100
to enhance performance.
However, the performance

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.429
enhancement was only about 2% —
just a few seconds.

00:02:50.429 --> 00:02:52.860
But check out this study.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.920
The same general strategy:
more fruits and vegetables,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.800
and less the acid-promoting
foods such as meats, cheeses,

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.040
and refined grains. But they
weren't messing around.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.860
Six to eight cups of vegetables,

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.160
plus more than four
servings of fruit a day, got

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.920
their urine up over 7, and a 21%
performance enhancement.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.020
That's extraordinary.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.260
Now this doesn't necessarily mean
it has anything to do with the pH.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.460
I mean they ate more vegetables,
which contain dietary nitrates,

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.120
which alone acutely improve
exercise performance.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.240
It's possible that nitrates
might have enhanced

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.580
exercise performance
during the low-acid trial.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.460
However, that would entail
extracting more energy

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.800
from every breath,
and they didn't find that.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.220
But any time you make huge
changes in peoples' diets,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.940
it's hard to pinpoint exactly what
made the critical difference.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.420
But these extra benefits
are a feature, not a bug.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.080
Because a more alkaline-forming
diet is rich in fruits and vegetables,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.920
and deplete of many unhealthy foods,
a low-acid diet could not only provide

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.320
exercise performance benefits, but
might also reduce chronic disease risk.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.100
Any performance benefits
in non-athletes?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:09.060
The effect of an alkaline diet
on body composition

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.420
and aerobic exercise performance
of sedentary women.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.140
A randomized controlled trial,
swapping in vegetable protein

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:21.531
sources like legumes for
animal protein sources, and...

00:04:21.531 --> 00:04:26.220
a greater decrease in weight, body
fat mass, lactic acid accumulation,

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.580
and perceived exertion levels,
all the while exhibiting a boost

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.240
in exercise performance
duration and VO2 max levels,

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.740
which is a measure of fitness.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.060
Again pH could just be one of many
explanations why eating healthier

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.640
could make you perform
better, but either way

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.360
we should recommend athletes
of all ages focus on consuming

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.731
ample amounts of fruits and vegetables,
if only to maintain long-term health.

